  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nHot and increasingly humid conditions remain likely on Sunday,\nahead of a weak cool front that will begin to make its way into\nthe area late Sunday and into Sunday night. Moisture is expected\nto pool along the boundary by the afternoon and along with \ntemperatures that should be comparable to the last few days, heat\nindex values should be noticeably higher due to the locally higher\ndew points. As such, the same areas that were upgraded to an\nExtreme Heat Warning today were also upgraded for tomorrow from\nNoon to 8 pm. Isolated to scattered thunderstorms remain expected\nto develop late afternoon and into the evening in the vicinity of\nthe boundary in northeast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas, with \ngreater coverage likely just north and east of the area near a \ndisturbance. Forecast soundings support a low chance of locally \ndamaging winds during the afternoon with the stronger storms. \n\nThe front will sag southward tomorrow night and into Monday, with\nlow chances for showers and storms extending roughly to the I-40 \ncorridor Monday afternoon. Noticeably cooler conditions should be \nexpected for the northern half of the forecast area Monday, with \nparts of southeast Oklahoma and the Arkansas River Valley hanging \non the extreme heat. Additional heat headlines will be needed for \nsome of the forecast area on Monday but with confidence low in the\nexact northern cut off for that need, will push that decision \nanother shift or two in the future. \n\nVery hot weather returns northward for Tuesday, with areawide \nheat headlines likely needed into Wednesday. A very low chance of\nanother round of showers and thunderstorms in far northeast \nOklahoma and northwest Arkansas exists Tuesday, although the \nbetter potential remains north of the area. The NBM POPs have been\nadjusted upward into the double digits but still below \nmentionable. \n\nLate in the week, models continue to show the upper level high\nshifting westward, with periods of northwest flow developing\nacross the area. This would favor cooler temperatures and at least\na brief break in the triple digit heat in much of the area, as \nwell as shower and thunderstorm chances. Ensemble data do show a\ncontinued wobble in where the high is centered, with occasional\nextensions back into our area beyond the end of this forecast\nperiod.",
